# Soft Beats

The default scaffold. The orchestrator may drop, replace, reorder, or invent soft beats when it serves pacing. Soft beats may be promoted to hard with the user's explicit approval.

IDs use the form `S-<short-slug>`.

## Format

Same as `hard.md`. Soft beats are typically scene-level pacing, character interaction, voice-establishment, or pacing brakes that the source delivers but the rewrite has discretion over.

## Beats

---

### S-EXAMPLE — [Short title]
- **Source**: source-book-N / ch.MM
- **Target arc / book**: arc-N / book-M
- **Description**: [What this beat would deliver. Pacing function, character interaction, voice register, etc.]
- **Status**: pending | dropped | landed (scene: <book-N/ch-MM/scene-PP>) | promoted-to-hard

[Add soft beats as you outline. Typically 50–200 soft beats across a multi-book project.]
